# Code Quality Standards - SLAM25 Project

## Core Quality Principles

This Poetry Slam members area follows **simplified code quality standards** that prioritize readability, maintainability, and consistency.

## Code Style Standards

### ✅ JavaScript/React Conventions
```javascript
// ✅ Use const/let, avoid var
const participants = await fetchParticipants();
let isLoading = false;

// ✅ Use arrow functions for callbacks
const handleClick = () => {
  setIsOpen(!isOpen);
};

// ✅ Use template literals
const message = `Welcome ${user.name}!`;

// ✅ Use destructuring
const { data, isLoading, error } = useQuery(['participants'], fetchParticipants);
```

### ✅ Component Naming
```javascript
// ✅ PascalCase for components
function ParticipantCard({ participant }) {
  return <div>{participant.name}</div>;
}

// ✅ camelCase for functions
function fetchParticipants() {
  return api.get('/participants');
}

// ✅ UPPER_CASE for constants
const API_BASE_URL = 'http://localhost:3005/api';
const POLLING_INTERVAL = 30000;
```

### ✅ File Naming
```
// ✅ kebab-case for files
participant-card.jsx
admin-dashboard.jsx
error-message.jsx

// ✅ camelCase for hooks
useParticipants.js
useError.js
useFormManager.js

// ✅ camelCase for services
authService.js
errorService.js
roundsService.js
```

## Code Organization

### ✅ Import Order
```javascript
// ✅ React imports first
import React, { useState, useEffect } from 'react';
import { useQuery } from '@tanstack/react-query';

// ✅ Third-party imports
import { useForm } from 'react-hook-form';
import { zodResolver } from '@hookform/resolvers/zod';

// ✅ Internal imports (alphabetical)
import { useAuth } from '../contexts/AuthContext.jsx';
import { useError } from '../hooks/useError.js';
import { fetchParticipants } from '../services/participantsService.js';
```

### ✅ Component Structure
```javascript
// ✅ Standard component structure
function ComponentName({ prop1, prop2 }) {
  // 1. Hooks
  const { data, isLoading } = useQuery(['key'], fetchFunction);
  const [localState, setLocalState] = useState(null);
  
  // 2. Event handlers
  const handleClick = () => {
    // Handle click
  };
  
  // 3. Effects
  useEffect(() => {
    // Side effects
  }, [dependency]);
  
  // 4. Early returns
  if (isLoading) return <LoadingSpinner />;
  if (error) return <ErrorMessage error={error} />;
  
  // 5. Render
  return (
    <div className="component-wrapper">
      {/* Component content */}
    </div>
  );
}
```

## Error Handling Standards

### ✅ Error Boundaries
```javascript
// ✅ Error boundary component
function ErrorBoundary({ children, fallback }) {
  const [hasError, setHasError] = useState(false);
  
  if (hasError) {
    return fallback || <ErrorMessage error="Something went wrong" />;
  }
  
  return children;
}
```

### ✅ Try-Catch Patterns
```javascript
// ✅ Async function error handling
const handleSubmit = async (data) => {
  try {
    const result = await submitData(data);
    setSuccessMessage('Data saved successfully');
  } catch (error) {
    handleError(error, { context: 'form_submission' });
  }
};
```

### ✅ Error Messages
```javascript
// ✅ User-friendly error messages
const getErrorMessage = (error) => {
  switch (error.code) {
    case 'VALIDATION_ERROR':
      return 'Please check your input and try again';
    case 'NETWORK_ERROR':
      return 'Network connection failed. Please try again';
    default:
      return 'An unexpected error occurred';
  }
};
```

## Performance Standards

### ✅ React Query Optimization
```javascript
// ✅ Optimized queries
const { data } = useQuery({
  queryKey: ['participants'],
  queryFn: fetchParticipants,
  staleTime: 5 * 60 * 1000, // 5 minutes
  cacheTime: 10 * 60 * 1000, // 10 minutes
  refetchInterval: 30000, // 30 seconds
  refetchOnWindowFocus: false
});
```

### ✅ Component Optimization
```javascript
// ✅ Memoization for expensive calculations
const expensiveValue = useMemo(() => {
  return participants.reduce((sum, p) => sum + p.score, 0);
}, [participants]);

// ✅ Callback memoization
const handleClick = useCallback(() => {
  setIsOpen(!isOpen);
}, [isOpen]);
```

### ✅ Lazy Loading
```javascript
// ✅ Lazy component loading
const AdminDashboard = lazy(() => import('./AdminDashboard.jsx'));

// ✅ Lazy route loading
const AdminRoutes = lazy(() => import('./AdminRoutes.jsx'));
```

## Database Standards

### ✅ Query Optimization
```javascript
// ✅ Use indexes
const participants = await executeQuery(
  'SELECT * FROM participants WHERE region = $1 ORDER BY name',
  [region]
);

// ✅ Limit results
const recentNews = await executeQuery(
  'SELECT * FROM news ORDER BY created_at DESC LIMIT 10',
  []
);
```

### ✅ Transaction Handling
```javascript
// ✅ Use transactions for related operations
const client = await pool.connect();
try {
  await client.query('BEGIN');
  
  const participant = await client.query(
    'INSERT INTO participants (name, region) VALUES ($1, $2) RETURNING *',
    [name, region]
  );
  
  await client.query(
    'INSERT INTO round_assignments (round_id, participant_id) VALUES ($1, $2)',
    [roundId, participant.rows[0].id]
  );
  
  await client.query('COMMIT');
} catch (error) {
  await client.query('ROLLBACK');
  throw error;
} finally {
  client.release();
}
```

