## Code Review Standards

### ✅ Review Checklist
- [ ] **Functionality** - Code works as expected
- [ ] **Performance** - No unnecessary re-renders or queries
- [ ] **Error Handling** - Proper error boundaries and try-catch
- [ ] **Accessibility** - Proper ARIA labels and keyboard navigation
- [ ] **Testing** - Adequate test coverage
- [ ] **Documentation** - Clear comments and documentation
- [ ] **Consistency** - Follows project conventions

### ✅ Common Issues to Avoid
```javascript
// ❌ DON'T use var
var participants = [];

// ❌ DON'T use function declarations in components
function ComponentName() {
  function handleClick() { // ❌ This creates a new function on every render
    // Handle click
  }
}

// ❌ DON'T mutate props
function Component({ data }) {
  data.name = 'New Name'; // ❌ Mutating props
}

// ❌ DON'T use array index as key
{participants.map((participant, index) => (
  <ParticipantCard key={index} participant={participant} />
))}
```

